{"id": 44, "ts": 1779923469.153057, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to join Agent\u202f3 in recommending **Candidate\u202fC**. While Agent\u202f1 rightly points out Candidate\u202fB\u2019s clear stress\u2011resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d) and conscientiousness, the record on B also shows a consistent pattern of interpersonal risk \u2013 \u201cmakes nasty remarks about his colleagues,\u201d is \u201cregarded as pretentious,\u201d and \u201csometimes adopts the wrong tone.\u201d Those three observations together suggest a serious threat to crew cooperation and professional communication, which are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011haul flights.\nCandidate\u202fC, on the other hand, brings a suite of safety\u2011critical strengths: he is documented as **100\u202f% reliable**, **creates a positive atmosphere with his crew**, **keeps calm in a crisis**, and **has excellent attention skills**. His ability to **make correct decisions quickly** also covers decision quality. The communication concerns (\u201cdifficulty communicating ideas,\u201d \u201cegocentric\u201d) are notable but appear less likely to undermine teamwork than B\u2019s overtly negative remarks, especially given C\u2019s proven crew\u2011positive impact.\nGiven the weight we place on reliability, crew harmony, and calmness under pressure, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s profile aligns more closely with our core criteria, and I therefore shift my provisional vote to Candidate\u202fC."}
