{"id": 52, "ts": 1779923531.5215502, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I concur with the emerging consensus around Candidate\u202fC.\u202fWhile we still lack direct observations of C\u2019s calmness under pressure, the record does show he \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d which implies the ability to act decisively in demanding moments\u2014a core element of stress resilience.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fD offers no concrete evidence of calmness or effective crisis performance; the only note is that he \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately,\u201d which falls short of the clear stress\u2011resilience signal we have for B or the decision\u2011quality signal for C.\u202fMoreover, D\u2019s \u201chot temper,\u201d being \u201cregarded as moody\u201d and a \u201cloner\u201d raise additional concerns for crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014areas where C already demonstrates strength with a \u201cpositive atmosphere with his crew.\u201d\u202fGiven C\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, excellent attention skills, and proven crew\u2011positive impact, his profile still aligns best with our safety\u2011critical criteria despite the communication\u2011style gaps.\u202fTherefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fC**."}
